  "description": "Details of Condition 3 (Hard and soft landscaping scheme) as required by full planning permission 23/AP/3112 dated 02/02/2024 for 'Variation of Condition 1 (Approved plans) to planning permission 18/AP/2840 'Variation of Condition 1 (Approved plans) of planning permission 15/AP/4337 (Creation of a new public square between Peckham Rye Station and Rye Lane following demolition of the arcade buildings currently located between the north and south railway viaducts; refurbishment of the railway arches facing onto the new square and refurbishment and erection of a two storey extension to the building at 2-10 Blenheim Grove / 82 Rye Lane, to provide A1 (retail), A2 (financial and professional), A3 (restaurant / cafe), A5 (hot food takeaway), B1a (offices) and D1 (non-residential institution) uses, together with hard landscaping, public WC and other associated works.) comprising\rIncrease in the overall height of extension by 500mm; \rReduction in plan size of Blenheim Grove extension;\rProvision of boundary fence along railway parapet wall;\rAlterations to elevations including location of windows, louvres and inclusion of fixed access ladder and Boundary fencing.' for the following amendments\r- Adjustments to the fenestration and shop fronts on the Blenheim Grove building\r- Adjustment and addition of ventilation louvres\r- Changes to the internal layouts\r- Former Use Classes A1, A2, A3, A5, B1a and D1 to be Use Classes\rE (Commercial, business and service) and F2 (Local community)\r- Modification of the number and location of columns beneath Platform 3 on the north side of the square\r- Modification of the platform screen forming the south face of Platform 3 at high level'",
